WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:13.500
INTRO:
5&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:29.700
people founded Tesla, but only&nbsp;
1 became a billionaire. Today,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:35.640
Tesla and Elon Musk are synonymous.&nbsp;
Elon has led the company since 2008,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:41.160
and it was under his leadership that the company&nbsp;
evolved from being a nearly bankrupt startup to a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:47.100
trillion dollar automotive giant. This has made&nbsp;
Elon the largest shareholder of Tesla owning a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:52.260
little less than 1/5th of the company which has&nbsp;
made him the richest man in the world by far. But,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:59.400
Elon wasn’t the only key player at Tesla. In fact,&nbsp;
he wasn’t even one of the original founders, yet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:05.400
he’s worth magnitudes more than any of the other&nbsp;
four founders. Only one of the other founders,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:11.760
JB Straubel, has even reached billionaire&nbsp;
status coming in at $1.3 billion. But,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:18.300
that was one year ago when Tesla stock was at its&nbsp;
peak. Since then, Tesla stock has sold off 48%,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:25.740
so it’s unlikely that JB is a billionaire&nbsp;
anymore. Obviously, this isn’t to say that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:31.560
other founders are not well off given that they’re&nbsp;
likely worth tens of millions if not hundreds of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:38.340
millions. But, when you compare those figures to&nbsp;
Elon’s $200 billion fortune, they’re nothing. Elon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:42.600
literally has daily net worth swings that are&nbsp;
worth more than the cumulative net worth of all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:49.680
the other founders combined. So, why is Elon Musk&nbsp;
the only Tesla cofounder that became stupid rich?

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:54.960
MONEY TALKS:
Taking a look back,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.960 --> 00:02:00.600
Tesla was originally founded by two men named&nbsp;
Martin Eberhard and Marc Tarpenning on July 1,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:06.900
2003. Martin served as the CEO of the company&nbsp;
while Marc served as the CFO. Their dream was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:11.280
to create a modern technology based automotive&nbsp;
company with a focus on batteries, computer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:16.860
software, and proprietary motors. But, while they&nbsp;
had high ambitions, something that they didn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:22.620
have was money. If this was an internet based&nbsp;
company or some sort of app, they may have been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:28.320
able to get away with bootstrapping it. But, given&nbsp;
that this was an automotive company, that just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:34.620
wasn’t gonna fly. So, they set out to raise money&nbsp;
almost instantaneously and they would close their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:39.900
Series A round of funding in February of 2004.&nbsp;
They would actually raise a substantial amount of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:47.520
money coming in at $6.5 million. But almost all of&nbsp;
that came from a single individual investor: Elon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:54.420
Musk. According to Elon, he invested $6.35 million&nbsp;
and Martin invested $75,000. Some other sources&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.420 --> 00:03:00.060
actually report that the initial funding round&nbsp;
was worth $7.5 million and that Compass Technology&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:05.280
Partners and a few others threw in the last&nbsp;
million. Either way though, Elon was by far the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:11.040
largest investor and he was far from being done.&nbsp;
In the meantime, Martin and Marc were building&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:16.200
out the initial Tesla team. The first person that&nbsp;
they hired was Ian Wright, and a couple of months&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:22.440
later, they would hire JB Straubel as CTO. Today,&nbsp;
these five men are the ones that are credited with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:28.380
founding Tesla. Elon was definitely an involved&nbsp;
investor from day one as he played an active role&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:34.020
in the development of the original Tesla Roadster.&nbsp;
But, he wasn’t quite an employee per se given that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:38.460
he wasn’t that involved in the companies daily&nbsp;
activities. That didn’t really matter though&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:44.160
because by far Elon’s largest contribution to&nbsp;
Tesla in the early days was capital, and let’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:49.680
just say, he kept the capital flowing. About 2&nbsp;
years after Series A, Elon would lead a Series B&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:55.320
funding round that ended up raising $13 million&nbsp;
and added Valor Equity Partners to the funding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.320 --> 00:04:01.140
team. And just 4 months after that, Elon would&nbsp;
co lead a Series C funding round that raised $40&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:06.060
million and got many of his tech friends involved&nbsp;
in Tesla. This included the cofounders of Google,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:12.300
Sergey Brin and Larry Page, as well as the former&nbsp;
president of eBay, Jeff Skoll. Elon would finally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:17.400
round off all the fundraising with a fourth round&nbsp;
of funding that raised $45 million. These were all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:22.680
the funding rounds the Elon happily engaged in,&nbsp;
but there was actually one more unexpected round&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:29.220
of funding. The dark days of 2008 would force Elon&nbsp;
to put everything else he had into the company and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:35.520
by the time the company got to the other side,&nbsp;
they had raised a total of $187 million. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:40.920
marked the end of Elon’s personal contributions&nbsp;
and VC funding rounds. Since then, Tesla has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:45.840
primarily relied on the governments, other car&nbsp;
companies, and public investors for capital. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:52.680
fortunately, none of these have required too much&nbsp;
dilution. This left Elon with a ginormous 28.4%&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:58.980
stake at IPO. Meanwhile, the original founders&nbsp;
were essentially diluted into oblivion especially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:03.720
because they weren’t able to contribute much to&nbsp;
these funding rounds themselves. Neither Martin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:08.220
nor Marc have ever revealed details regarding&nbsp;
their Tesla stake during this time period but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:13.380
it was likely in the single digits. That’s&nbsp;
nothing to scoff at though. Even a 5% stake&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:19.620
in the company would be worth $34 billion. So,&nbsp;
how did Martin and Marc go from being future deca&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:25.860
billionaires to not even billionaires? Well, that&nbsp;
can be explained by the ousting of the founders.

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:29.820
FIRING THE FOUNDERS:
Elon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:36.600
Musk fanboys usually like to pretend that this&nbsp;
never happened. Meanwhile, Elon Musk haters like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:42.420
to frame this as Elon being the greedy investor&nbsp;
who wanted more power. But, in reality, neither&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.420 --> 00:05:47.820
of these are what really happened. The truth&nbsp;
was that Martin and Marc were hitting some brick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:53.760
walls when it came to running Tesla, and this was&nbsp;
becoming increasingly apparent. Martin had set up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:59.400
a rather inefficient supply chain that encompassed&nbsp;
three continents. First, much of the roadster’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:04.620
parts and materials were sourced from all over&nbsp;
Asia. Then, it was assembled and safety tested&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:11.100
in England. And finally, it had to be shipped to&nbsp;
North America to be delivered. This was obviously&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:16.200
not very efficient and it made the production&nbsp;
cost of the roadster far higher than the purchase&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:22.620
price. Martin didn’t really want to admit this, so&nbsp;
he allegedly misled investors regarding how much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:27.420
the Roadster would cost to produce. Elon claims&nbsp;
that Martin assured him that the Roadster would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:33.780
cost $65,000 after the first 100 units. However,&nbsp;
knowing how inefficient Tesla’s supply chain was,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:40.260
Elon was sus of these numbers. So, he ordered a&nbsp;
detailed cost breakdown of the car and it turned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.260 --> 00:06:47.400
out that it was closer to $120,000. Apparently,&nbsp;
even that was being generous. By the time they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:53.280
actually got past the first 100 units, the&nbsp;
materials alone were costing them $140,000 per&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.280 --> 00:07:00.000
car. For obvious reasons, Musk was triggered and&nbsp;
moved to fire Martin. The right way to approach&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:04.980
this situation would have been to setup a meeting&nbsp;
Martin and hash out their differences. Martin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:10.200
claims that he was well aware of his shortcomings&nbsp;
and that he himself had brought up the idea of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:15.420
bringing in a more experienced CEO to replace him.&nbsp;
So, I’m sure they could’ve come to an amicable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.420 --> 00:07:20.880
solution if they had just set up a meeting. But&nbsp;
instead, Elon decided to arrange a shareholder&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:25.860
coup while Martin was attending a business meeting&nbsp;
outside the country. And Elon wouldn’t even inform&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.860 --> 00:07:30.900
Martin until after the deed was done. As you&nbsp;
would guess, when Martin heard about this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:37.020
he too was triggered, and this has led to the&nbsp;
great feud between them ever since. Apparently,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.020 --> 00:07:43.080
Elon offered Martin a position as an advisor,&nbsp;
but it seems that Martin took this as more of an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:48.840
insult than an opportunity. All of this transpired&nbsp;
during the summer of 2007, and Martin and Marc&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.840 --> 00:07:54.540
would both leave Tesla altogether at the beginning&nbsp;
of 2008. They would turn around and sue Elon for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:59.100
forcing them out, but they would eventually&nbsp;
settle. The full details of the settlement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:03.480
were not revealed, but one of the agreements&nbsp;
that they came to was that all of them would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:09.900
credited as co founders of Tesla, and that’s how&nbsp;
Elon Musk, JB Straubel, and Ian Wright officially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.900 --> 00:08:15.540
became co founders. Ian had already left Tesla&nbsp;
on his own will just one year after joining,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.540 --> 00:08:21.600
so he obviously didn’t have a very big stake&nbsp;
in Tesla. Martin and Marc likely did though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:26.820
and the only reason they’re not deca billionaires&nbsp;
today is because they sold the majority of their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.820 --> 00:08:33.120
stakes, likely out of spite. And that leaves&nbsp;
us with just JB Straubel and Elon Musk.

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:36.900
AGGRESSIVE CEO COMPENSATION:&nbsp;

00:08:36.900 --> 00:08:42.420
Elon’s aggressive funding rounds no doubt played&nbsp;
a massive role in his multi hundred billion dollar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.420 --> 00:08:48.000
fortune, but that’s not the only ingredient.&nbsp;
Something else that has put him far ahead of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:54.240
other founders is his aggressive CEO compensation.&nbsp;
Musk often likes to claim that his compensation is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.240 --> 00:09:01.440
only $1 per year and while that may be technically&nbsp;
true, it means absolutely nothing. For someone as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:07.020
rich as Elon, no company can afford to pay him&nbsp;
a cash salary that’s worth his time. Even if a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.020 --> 00:09:12.240
company paid him $200 million per year like Sundar&nbsp;
Pichai, it would take him a thousand years to earn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:18.780
his current fortune, and that’s before taxes.&nbsp;
So, the only way Elon can be compensated is stock&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:25.680
compensation, and oh boy, his stock compensation&nbsp;
is nuts. His latest compensation plan was created&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.680 --> 00:09:32.040
in 2018 when Tesla was worth $59 billion. The&nbsp;
plan entailed Elon getting an additional 1%&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:37.860
of the company for every $50 billion increment in&nbsp;
marketcap. To offset for euphoric stock runs like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.860 --> 00:09:42.960
we saw over the past two years, Elon also has to&nbsp;
achieve certain revenue and earnings milestones as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:48.720
well. For Elon to unlock the entire compensation&nbsp;
which is worth 12%, he has to hit a market cap&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.720 --> 00:09:57.060
of $650 billion, annual revenue of $175 billion,&nbsp;
and an adjusted EBITA of $14 billion. Tesla has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.060 --> 00:10:03.900
already achieved a marketcap of $650 billion&nbsp;
and an EBITA of $14 billion. So, he just has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.900 --> 00:10:09.180
to hit the revenue targets. This will definitely&nbsp;
take some time given that Tesla still has to grow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.180 --> 00:10:13.860
their revenue by a $100 billion from where they&nbsp;
are today. But, given their current trajectory,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:19.200
I think it’s reasonable to estimate that they’ll&nbsp;
crush that number by the end of this decade by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:24.960
which point Elon would have grown his Tesla&nbsp;
stake by a whopping 12%. If Tesla is worth $3&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.960 --> 00:10:31.740
trillion at that time, Elon’s compensation would&nbsp;
have been worth a mind boggling $360 billion.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.740 --> 00:10:37.920
Not to mention, that’ll just keep growing with&nbsp;
time. If Tesla does hit a $10 trillion valuation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:44.580
like many Tesla bulls are hoping for, Elon’s&nbsp;
compensation would be worth $1.2 trillion. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:50.160
you might be wondering how Tesla’s board approved&nbsp;
such a generous compensation plan. Well, while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:55.020
this numbers are ludicrous from an individual’s&nbsp;
perspective, they’re not that crazy compared to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.020 --> 00:11:00.540
Tesla’s growth. When Elon pitched this idea in&nbsp;
2018, this is essentially what he was asking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.540 --> 00:11:07.140
for. Would it be possible for everyone to dilute&nbsp;
their shares by 12% and give it to me if I 13X the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:12.840
company in the coming years. Taking such a deal&nbsp;
is a no brainer. If Elon doesn’t hit his goals,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.840 --> 00:11:18.060
you don’t even have pay him. If he does hit his&nbsp;
goals though, both of you would have ridiculous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.060 --> 00:11:23.040
gains. Now of course, there are some shareholders&nbsp;
that are mad and have even filed a lawsuit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:30.240
against Elon and Tesla, but this is definitely the&nbsp;
minority. And that brings us to JB Straubel. Even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:30.240 --> 00:11:36.240
though JB was a cofounder, he was never CEO and so&nbsp;
he never had access to such generous compensation.

00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:42.300
WHY ONLY ELON IS RICH:
Whether you think it’s fair or not,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:47.100
the reason that Elon is magnitudes richer&nbsp;
than Tesla’s other founders is because he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:47.100 --> 00:11:52.620
played his cards extremely well. Elon leveraged&nbsp;
his position to the absolute maximum every step&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.620 --> 00:11:58.200
of the way. When he was an investor, he led every&nbsp;
single funding round and put in every penny he had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:58.200 --> 00:12:03.960
into the company, maximizing his stake. Then,&nbsp;
when he became CEO, he slashed his salary to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:03.960 --> 00:12:08.820
the absolute minimum so that he could maximize&nbsp;
his stock compensation. We should also mention&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.820 --> 00:12:13.800
that Elon’s current Tesla stake only accounts&nbsp;
for about half of his net worth. The rest of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.800 --> 00:12:18.780
his net worth comes from SpaceX and potentially&nbsp;
Twitter by the time your watching this. Meanwhile,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.780 --> 00:12:23.940
the remaining Tesla founders never had the&nbsp;
leverage of capital and/or they made some missteps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:23.940 --> 00:12:29.220
along the way that pushed them out of the company&nbsp;
altogether. Given their situation, they should’ve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:34.920
started a much cheaper business if getting rich&nbsp;
was their goal. But, honestly, I don’t think they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:34.920 --> 00:12:39.900
mind too much. While they’re not billionaires and&nbsp;
definitely not centibillionaires, they’re still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.740 --> 00:12:47.820
extremely well off. And though they may not be as&nbsp;
rich or as popular as Elon, there’s no doubt that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:47.820 --> 00:12:53.580
their real world impacts are far larger than what&nbsp;
their net worths may suggest. Do you think Elon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:59.340
stole Tesla? Comment that down below. Also, drop&nbsp;
a like if you’re glad that Tesla is doing well and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:59.340 --> 00:13:04.020
electrifying the world. And of course, consider&nbsp;
checking out our discord community to suggest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:04.020 --> 00:13:07.740
future video ideas and consider subscribing&nbsp;
